1
00:00:10,481 --> 00:00:13,361
When cannons get tired - the birds start to sing.

2
00:00:13,441 --> 00:00:16,142
When rates fall - belief starts to breathe.

3
00:00:16,162 --> 00:00:17,322
The world didn’t end.

4
00:00:18,542 --> 00:00:20,442
It just pressed pause.

5
00:00:21,522 --> 00:00:24,043
The Fed taps brakes in a quiet tone,

6
00:00:24,063 --> 00:00:26,763
The economy coughs - but it’s still alive.

7
00:00:26,783 --> 00:00:29,343
Two point five - it’s not just a number,

8
00:00:29,363 --> 00:00:32,183
It’s the world coming back from the static noise.

9
00:00:32,343 --> 00:00:34,904
The war goes silent, gas flows through pipes,

10
00:00:35,264 --> 00:00:38,044
Sunset leans on an old jazz night.

11
00:00:38,084 --> 00:00:40,104
Some say it all went just as planned,

12
00:00:40,124 --> 00:00:43,045
I say we simply woke up too early, man.

13
00:00:43,445 --> 00:00:45,805
Two point five - it sounds like life,

14
00:00:46,065 --> 00:00:48,525
Rates go down, so do sharp thoughts and knives.

15
00:00:48,625 --> 00:00:51,885
The world falls asleep like a child in dreams,

16
00:00:52,406 --> 00:01:00,286
It’s over - and that’s both fear and relief.

17
00:01:04,887 --> 00:01:07,407
Finance breathes, but without the scream,

18
00:01:07,887 --> 00:01:10,107
Markets rise - no panic scene.

19
00:01:10,627 --> 00:01:12,608
People return to bread and light,

20
00:01:12,628 --> 00:01:15,588
To what existed before online life.

21
00:01:16,088 --> 00:01:18,228
Biden smiles like he knew it all,

22
00:01:18,368 --> 00:01:20,949
Behind that smile - a trading floor.

23
00:01:21,089 --> 00:01:23,429
The rate went down, but truth remained,

24
00:01:23,969 --> 00:01:26,389
We were just tired, stretched and strained.

25
00:01:26,769 --> 00:01:29,169
Two point five - it sounds like life,

26
00:01:29,429 --> 00:01:31,790
Rates go down, so do sharp thoughts and knives.

27
00:01:31,950 --> 00:01:34,490
The world falls asleep like a child in dreams,

28
00:01:34,510 --> 00:01:43,351
It’s over - and that’s both fear and relief.

29
00:01:48,451 --> 00:01:50,772
Frontlines filed into archive rows,

30
00:01:50,912 --> 00:01:53,752
Loans into charts, emotions froze.

31
00:01:53,812 --> 00:01:56,132
Some count profits off broken land,

32
00:01:56,492 --> 00:01:58,873
Some just follow the nearest hand.

33
00:01:59,233 --> 00:02:01,573
I don’t accuse - I just inhale,

34
00:02:01,713 --> 00:02:04,593
Where rates fall, I smell the spring in the air.

35
00:02:04,633 --> 00:02:07,273
Two point five - like fate’s deep breath,

36
00:02:07,313 --> 00:02:09,734
No gunshots - but a dream survives.

37
00:02:09,874 --> 00:02:12,234
The world wasn’t saved - just released,

38
00:02:12,314 --> 00:02:15,354
And that’s the miracle: we lived, we loved, we breathed.

39
00:02:15,374 --> 00:02:17,654
A rate’s not a number - it’s a sign of rest,

40
00:02:17,995 --> 00:02:21,015
The moment we finally became ourselves again.

41
00:02:23,535 --> 00:02:26,095
Two point five - and things feel aligned,

42
00:02:26,255 --> 00:02:28,776
Not a victory, but still dignified.

43
00:02:28,836 --> 00:02:31,176
We made it through, my brother, it’s true,

44
00:02:31,476 --> 00:02:34,836
Rates go down - and the soul floats too.

